From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: denchiklut <ollylut@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:15:38 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] oa: recycle a page view's compositor, as ArcCore does

Restores ui::RecyclableCompositorMacFactory, which upstream removed: a BrowserCompositorMac that leaves HasOwnCompositor gives its RecyclableCompositorMac to a pool of at most one spare, and the next one that enters it takes that spare instead of building a new compositor. Only a page's view (WebContentsViewMac::CreateViewForWidget) recycles; popups build their own, as in ArcCore, whose RenderWidgetHostViewMac and BrowserCompositorMac take the same added flag. An embedder that hosts the page's NSView itself, outside views' parent ui::Layer, otherwise shows nothing on every tab switch until the new compositor's first frame. BrowserCompositorMac::DisableRecyclingForShutdown() empties the pool before the context factory goes.
